-         A diff which deletes or keeps beyond the end of the sequence it is applied to panics:
-         it was computed against a different original.
-   entry #rdiff     pairs each deletion with a similar insertion as a substitution, giving an `RDiff`
+         Un diff que elimina o conserva más allá del final de la secuencia a la que se aplica
+         entra en pánico: se calculó contra un original distinto.
+   entry #rdiff     empareja cada eliminación con una inserción parecida como sustitución, y da un `RDiff`

=   entry #rdiff     pairs each deletion with a similar insertion as a substitution, giving an `RDiff`
-     detail
+     detail

-         `diff.rdiff(similar)` looks at each changed region of the diff (each `Tract.Changed`)
-         and, where it both deletes and inserts, pairs deletions with insertions as `Sub`s.
-         Within a region, the pairing is itself a diff of the deleted elements against the
-         inserted ones, with `similar` as the comparison, so as many similar pairs as possible
-         are found, in order; those left over stay as plain `Del`s and `Ins`s.
+         `diff.rdiff(similar)` examina cada región con cambios del diff (cada `Tract.Changed`)
+         y, donde elimina e inserta a la vez, empareja eliminaciones con inserciones como `Sub`.
+         Dentro de una región, el emparejamiento es a su vez un diff de los elementos eliminados
+         contra los insertados, con `similar` como comparación, de modo que se encuentran tantos
+         pares parecidos como sea posible, en orden; los que sobran quedan como `Del` e `Ins`
+         simples.

=         are found, in order; those left over stay as plain `Del`s and `Ins`s.
=
-         ```scala
+         ```scala

=         are found, in order; those left over stay as plain `Del`s and `Ins`s.
=
=         ```scala
-         import soundness.*
