- entry .Retained   the type-level proof that every edit of a diff carries its element
-     `Retained` is a refinement, `Any { type Retain = true }`, which marks an `Diff.Edit` or a
-     `Diff` whose values are known to be present. `diff` and `Redraft#resolve` return a
-     `Diff[element] & Retained`; a diff read from the unix format, or built by hand, does
-     not. Being a refinement rather than a trait, the mark costs nothing at runtime: an
-     `Diff.Edit[Text] & Retained` is an `Diff.Edit` like any other.
+ entry .Retained   la prueba a nivel de tipos de que cada edición de un diff lleva su elemento
+     `Retained` es un refinamiento, `Any { type Retain = true }`, que marca un `Diff.Edit` o un
+     `Diff` cuyos valores se sabe que están presentes. `diff` y `Redraft#resolve` devuelven un
+     `Diff[element] & Retained`; un diff leído del formato de unix, o construido a mano, no. Al
+     ser un refinamiento y no un trait, la marca no cuesta nada en tiempo de ejecución: un
+     `Diff.Edit[Text] & Retained` es un `Diff.Edit` como cualquier otro.

-     Two operations need the proof. `kept` reads an edit's value as a bare element instead of
-     an `Optional`, and `Diff.redraft` renders a diff as a `Redraft`, which must reproduce every
-     kept and deleted line.
+     Dos operaciones necesitan la prueba. `kept` lee el valor de una edición como un elemento
+     desnudo en lugar de como un `Optional`, y `Diff.redraft` representa un diff como un
+     `Redraft`, que debe reproducir cada línea conservada y eliminada.

